    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of the Foreign Contribution (Regulation) Act, 2010\nKey Provisions\n1.\tDefinitions \n•\tForeign Contribution: Donations, currency, securities, or hospitality from foreign sources.\n•\tForeign Hospitality: Non-casual offers of travel, boarding, etc., from foreign sources.\n•\tForeign Source: Includes foreign governments, international agencies, foreign companies, etc.\n2.\tRegulation of Foreign Contribution & Hospitality\n•\tProhibitions and Restrictions:\n•\tOrganisations of Political Nature: Designation process outlined, emphasizing transparency and due process.\n•\tRestrictions on Foreign Hospitality: Prohibits acceptance without prior Central Government permission, with exceptions for emergency medical aid.\n•\tProhibition on Transfer of Foreign Contributions: Strict ban on transferring received foreign contributions to other persons.\n•\tLimitations on Administrative Expenses : Caps administrative expenses to 20% of foreign contributions, with possibilities for approval of excess.\n3.\tRegistration, Prior Permission, and Reporting\n•\tRegistration Requirement: Mandatory for consistent foreign contribution recipients, with a streamlined 5-year renewal process.\n•\tPrior Permission: Required for non-registered entities, with a clarified application process for specific purposes or sources.\n•\tFCRA Account and Reporting: Mandatory account with specified banking channels; tightened reporting timelines, especially for election candidates (within 180 days before nomination).\n4.\tPower of Central Government\n•\tSpecification of Organisations of Political Nature: Detailed process for designation, including notice, representation, and decision timelines (up to 180 days).\n•\tProhibition and Regulation Powers: Authority to prohibit foreign contributions or hospitality based on national interest, public interest, electoral fairness, foreign relations, or social harmony.\n•\tExemption Power: Central Government can exempt entities in the public interest.\n5.\tCompliance and Penalties\n•\tEnhanced Audit Powers: With confidentiality for information obtained.\n•\tPenalties for Non-Compliance: Includes suspension, cancellation of registration, and legal action for violations.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
